{"strongs": "H5553", "word": "סֶ֫לַע", "translit": "se.la", "root": "סלע", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "crag, cliff", "definition": "I. סֶ֫לַע 61 noun masculine Judg 6:20 crag, cliff , synonym צוּר ; — absolute ׳ ס Judg 6:20 +, סָ֑לַע Num 20:10 +; construct סֶ֫לַע 1Sam 23:28 suffix סַלְעִי 2Sam 22:2 +, סַלְעוֺ Isa 31:9 plural סְלָעִים Isa 2:21 +; — 1. literally cliff, crag Judg 6:20 ; Isa 2:21 ; Isa 7:19 ; Amos 6:12 ; Num 20:8 (twice in verse); Num 20:10 (twice in verse); Num 20:11 (compare Neh 9:15 ; Ps 78:16 , and contrast the צוּר of Exod 17:6 ), Num 24:21 ; Deut 32:13 (not elsewhere Hexateuch), + 10 t.; ׳ שֵׁן הַסּ 1Sam 14:4 (twice in verse) tooth of the crag , i.e. sharp crag, so Job 39:28 excavated in cliff as place of burial Isa 22:16 abode of wild animals, ׳ יַעֲלֵיסֿ v Isa 22:1 , compare Ps 104:18 ; Prov 30:26 , of birds Job 39:28 ; Song 2:14 (in figurative), compare Jer 48:28 , so of Edom Obad 1:3 = Jer 49:16 compare ( Num 24:21 above and) Isa 42:11 particular cliffs are: עֵיטָם ׳ ס Judg 15:8 ; Judg 15:11 compare v Judg 15:13 , (הָ)רִמּוֺן ׳ ס Judg 20:45 ; Judg 20:47 (twice in verse); Judg 21:13 הַמַּחְלְקוֺת ׳ ס 1Sam 23:28 compare v 1Sam 23:25 see also II. סֶלַע . 2. figurative, especially סַלְעִי of ׳ י (only Psalms), Ps 18:3 = 2Sam 22:2 ; Ps 31:4 ; Ps 42:10 ; Ps 71:3 of Assyrian god Isa 31:9 (probably; compare צוּר Deut 32:31 ; Deut 32:37 ); כָּבֵד ׳ צֵל ס Isa 32:2 (simile of protecting care); figurative of security Ps 40:3 (feet on cliff), מְצָדוֺת סְלָעִים מִשְׂגַּבּוֺ Isa 33:16 symbol of obstinacy ׳ חִזְּקוּ פְנֵיהֶם מִסּ Jer 5:3 ׳ צְחִיחַ ס ( bare cliff , literally glare of [ the ] cliff ), in figure of openness, flagrancy Ezek 24:7 ; Ezek 24:8 , of razed city Ezek 26:4 ; Ezek 26:14 (only here Ezekiel); in figure of fall of Babylonian Jer 51:25 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5622')\">BDB5622</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5553')\">H5553</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB